<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113706" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χειρουργ-ός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>working</i> or <i>doing
				by hand,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.564e
			</span></i>: <i>practising a handicraft</i> or <i>art,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ γραφικήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>NA</u>
					17.9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ χ.</span>”
				<i>artificers, artists,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>VH</u>
					14.47
				</span></i>
			, etc.; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. τέχναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lib.
					<u>Or.</u>
					25.36
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χειρουργός, ὁ,</span>
			<i>surgeon,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.486c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Tetr.</u>
				180
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				10.455
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Artem.
				4.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				11.280
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Pall.
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
